# D-159 — WHICH SOURCE TREES EXIST, DERIVED OVER THE PLUGIN TREE RATHER THAN
# EXTENDED BY HAND AT THE SITE THAT REPORTED THE LAST GAP.
#
# THE AXIS. Every package-wide rule in test_spawn_progress.py asks two
# questions about membership, and only one of them was derived:
#
#   WITHIN a root   rglob. Bare read_text plants in parsers/, in a brand-new
#                   subpackage, and two directories deep are all named. PROVE
#                   could not break this one.
#   OF the roots    a two-element list. `plugins/foundry/scripts` was in it
#                   only because D-141 reported the D-137 document-load rule
#                   sitting inside the package boundary, and the fix added
#                   that one directory.
#
# THE HARM, driven by PROVE at cycle 21. A faithful full-repo plantbed with
# `plugins/foundry/lib/reader.py` carrying FOUR violations at once — an
# unguarded strict-decoding `path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")`, a raw
# `json.loads(text)` with no handler, a `print("planted reader tally: 3")`,
# and an unlocked `tmp.rename(dest)` onto a run artifact:
#
#   control (unplanted)   597 passed, 1 skipped
#   with the plant        597 passed, 1 skipped     <- BYTE-IDENTICAL
#
# and no test naming the file. Being outside every root and being clean were
# the same observation, so nothing had anything to say. There is no live
# instance today — every .py under plugins/foundry/ happens to sit in one of
# the two roots — which is exactly why it went unnoticed: the hole is that
# nothing REPORTS a shipped directory falling outside.
#
# THE FIX IS ON THE CLASS, NOT THE SITE. The roots are walked out of the
# plugin tree now, so a new top-level directory is judged by every rule that
# rides the shared helper — including the two package-wide rules in this
# module AND the scans in the other two test modules that import
# `_scanned_roots`/`_scanned_modules` from it. Both ORIGINAL roots keep their
# identity AND their position, because both are contracts: [0] is the
# importable package, [-1] is the hyphenated CLI tree that
# test_orchestrator_gates.py addresses positionally.
#
# Whatever is still outside is REPORTED rather than absent, and pinned
# two-sided against a declared exemption map carrying the reason — the shape
# test_evidence.py#test_no_module_declares_its_own_requirement_id_grammar
# already uses for offenders outside its grant. A new shipped directory now
# fails BY NAME.
#
# WHICH TREES ARE NOT SHIPPED is derived too, off the repository's own
# .gitignore rather than typed here. `.venv` holds several thousand
# third-party modules and exists only where somebody has run `uv`;
# `__pycache__` comes and goes with the last test run. A census that let
# either in would render differently in the working tree and in the detached
# worktree this gate builds — which is D-152/D-161's failure, one axis over.
#
# The plant below runs against a temporary tree, not the shipped one: two
# other castings run this suite against the same working tree, and a module
# that exists for four seconds inside src/foundry_mcp is a spurious offender
# in somebody else's run.
#
